{"dossier":"D09","entry_points":[{"sids":["arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::arch_setup_additional_pages","arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::compat_arch_setup_additional_pages","arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::load_vdso32","arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::vdso_setup"],"text":"Creation picks VDSO image by build, compat and enable controls, with 64-bit, 32-bit and extended paths and disabled fast returns."},{"sids":["arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::emulate_vsyscall_pf","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::emulate_vsyscall_gp","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::addr_to_vsyscall_nr","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_is_processor_usable","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_parse_lapic_addr_ovr","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/apei.c::arch_apei_report_x86_error"],"text":"Fault helpers enter vsyscall emulation after user, fetch and range checks. CPU usability follows enabled, online-capable or legacy-guest rules. Addr override adopts LAPIC base. CPU errors forward to SMCA."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_parse_ioapic","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_parse_int_src_ovr","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_parse_nmi_src","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_sci_ioapic_setup","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_pic_sci_set_trigger"],"text":"IOAPIC entries pick legacy or dynamic domains and register. Overrides record receipt, divert control IRQs, fix timer and polarity, else apply. NMI only validates and logs. Control defaults level and low, honours overrides, registers, penalises, stores; PIC sets trigger bits."}],"exports":[{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c::text_poke_early","arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::vdso_fault"],"text":"Early patch writes bytes to kernel or module text, direct for non-executable module text, otherwise IRQ-suppressed with serialization. VDSO faults map offsets to pages with refs held."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::mce_prep_record","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::mce_log","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/apei.c::apei_mce_report_mem_error","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/apei.c::apei_smca_report_x86_error"],"text":"MCE prep clears then fills identity. Logging pools records, announces and defers work on success. Firmware memory errors become memory-read records with address, granularity and severity flags. SMCA validates support, address, size and LAPIC match, fills fixed slots up to a cap, then logs."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/apic/probe_64.c::default_acpi_madt_oem_check","arch/x86/kernel/apic/init.c::apic_install_driver","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::mp_register_ioapic","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::mp_find_ioapic","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::mp_find_ioapic_pin","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::mpc_ioapic_id","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::mp_save_irq","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::mp_register_ioapic_irq","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::mp_override_legacy_irq","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::mp_config_acpi_gsi","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_isa_irq_to_gsi","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_gsi_to_irq","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_register_gsi"],"text":"APIC installs first driver matching OEM IDs, adjusts max ID and announces routing. IOAPIC registry adds units, maps globals to unit and pin, shows IDs. Sources append with dup suppression; ISA and PCI record bus entries; legacy overrides validate, fix timer trigger and refresh ISA map; GSI helpers translate globals to IRQs."}],"extracts":["1c0e88fe19dba548bb408d4c6acdfa373a0a9b7c8c4c423b9ae2c415a7bca2a1","3d958b136ab6a892be716f6ecde441f9d2d8a2b36442ea76ca883fa4dc41ca51","d875d08aa72a0b01949e477f8a7993c32c3fe11aaab832ac086794f17e76000d"],"gpl_spec":"PASS","hazards":[{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c::alt_replace_call","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::warn_bad_vsyscall","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::__emulate_vsyscall","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::write_ok_or_segv"],"text":"Call swap needs short direct and longer indirect shapes; mismatch aborts, missing uses bug handler, NOP suppresses. Bad emulation rate-limited warns and signals on bad stack, misalignment, unwritable buffer or seccomp."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology.c::check_for_real_bsp"],"text":"Bootstrap uses hardware indicator else order, refuses foreign bootstrap, pins to one CPU on mismatch and reports order faults as firmware bugs."}],"invariants":[{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c::need_reloc","arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c::apply_reloc_n","arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c::optimize_nops","arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c::skip_nops","arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c::add_nop","arch/x86/kernel/alternative.c::patch_site.alt_2","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/cpuid-deps.c::do_clear_cpu_cap","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/cpuid-deps.c::clear_feature","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/cpuid-deps.c::clear_cpu_cap","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/cpuid-deps.c::setup_clear_cpu_cap","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/apei.c::arch_apei_enable_cmcff","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::mce_disable_bank","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/threshold.c::mce_save_apei_thr_limit","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/apei.c::arch_apei_report_mem_error"],"text":"Relocation adjusts only out-of-block targets under range check. Patch sites merge NOP runs and rewrite padding. CPU-bit clear cascades to dependents globally or per CPU. Firmware-first stores thresholds, needs flag and count, disables banks, forwards reports; bad bank IDs warn and return."},{"sids":["arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::vdso_mremap","arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::vdso_fix_landing","arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::map_vdso_once","arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::arch_syscall_is_vdso_sigreturn","arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::vvar_vclock_fault","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::set_vsyscall_pgtable_user_bits"],"text":"VDSO move rebases in-flight threads and refreshes bases. One VDSO family per process. Sigreturn only for 32-bit image at two offsets. Vclock faults need defined used modes and backing pages. Early vsyscall marks paging levels user-accessible."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::mce_prep_record_common","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::mce_prep_record_per_cpu","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/genpool.c::mce_gen_pool_add","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/amd.c::amd_filter_mce","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/amd.c::smca_get_bank_type","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/intel.c::intel_filter_mce"],"text":"Prep stores CPU, vendor, capability, time and per-CPU IDs. Pool vendor-filters, needs init, rate-limits faults, else copies and queues lock-free. AMD drops three errata classes fail-closed unknown; Intel drops one bank-zero pattern on few Haswell, Broadwell and Skylake parts."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_force","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_disabled","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_irq_model","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::isa_irq_to_gsi","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology.c::topo_register_apic","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology.c::topo_apicid","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology.c::topo_set_cpuids"],"text":"Boot tracks ACPI enable, IRQ model and ISA map with cleared force, PIC default and identity map. Registration marks present IDs, assigns zero to boot ID, stores APIC and ACPI IDs and updates domain maps raw low and masked above."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::mp_ioapic_gsi_routing","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::mp_ioapic_pin_count","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::find_irq_entry","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::irq_active_low","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::irq_is_level","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::__acpi_get_override_irq","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::acpi_get_override_irq"],"text":"Each IOAPIC owns a closed global interval; pin is offset and count is span. Override search finds first matching type, pin and dest, decodes flags with bus defaults, defaults edge and high on miss; a global flag can disable lookup."}],"locks":[{"sids":["arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::map_vdso","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_ioapic_lock"],"text":"VDSO install holds the address-space write lock, unwinding on failure. A static mutex exists for ACPI IOAPIC handling."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::io_apic_get_redir_entries","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::io_apic_get_version","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::io_apic_get_unique_id","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::io_apic_unique_id.alt_2","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::io_apic_unique_id.alt_1"],"text":"One IRQ-saving spinlock guards IOAPIC register groups for version, size and ID assignment. IDs stay unique via bitmap and scan with hardware program and verify, or via requested, hardware then free preference."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F2"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::vsyscall_setup","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::map_vsyscall","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::__ro_after_init.alt_1","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::anon_1"],"text":"Vsyscall mode is boot-chosen among emulate, execute-only and none, gating backing page and gate visibility."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/core.c::filter_mce","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/internal.h::intel_filter_mce","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mce/internal.h::amd_filter_mce","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_parse_madt","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_parse_x2apic","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_check_lapic","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_parse_lapic","arch/x86/kernel/acpi/boot.c::acpi_parse_sapic","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/topology.c::topology_register_apic"],"text":"Filtering dispatches by boot vendor, accept-all when unbuilt. MADT needs APIC and mappable table, adopts LAPIC base, notes legacy, gates online-capable by revision, matches OEM. Entries validate, skip bad IDs and register rest. Topology rejects over-limit, foreign bootstrap and post-limit IDs, counting rejections."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::find_free_ioapic_entry","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::bad_ioapic_register","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::io_apic_set_fixmap"],"text":"Registration claims first zero-count entry, installs encrypted-aware fixmap, and tears down on all-ones registers."}],"structs":[{"sids":["arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::vdso_mapping","arch/x86/entry/vdso/vma.c::vvar_vclock_mapping","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::gate_vma_name","arch/x86/entry/vsyscall/vsyscall_64.c::gate_vma_ops"],"text":"Descriptors bind VDSO and vclock areas to fault handlers, VDSO also to move, with distinct names. Vsyscall gate is one fixed read-execute page with a name op."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::mp_irqdomain_create","arch/x86/kernel/apic/io_apic.c::alloc_ioapic_saved_registers"],"text":"IOAPIC entries build hierarchical domains sized by pins and allocate suspend buffers sized by register count."}],"stubs":[{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeature.h::cpu_feature_enabled","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/cpufeature.h::boot_cpu_has","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/insn.h::insn_decode_kernel","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/lib/insn-eval.c::insn_is_nop","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"include/linux/mmap_lock.h::mmap_write_unlock","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D06"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/fixmap.h::__set_fixmap","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/mce.h::mce_save_apei_thr_limit","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/page.h::__pa","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/page.h::__pa_symbol","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/page.h::virt_to_page","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/paravirt.h::__p4d","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/paravirt.h::__pgd","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/paravirt.h::__pmd","state":"stub","target_dossier":"D10"},{"sid":"arch/x86/include/asm/paravirt.h::__pud","state":"stub","target_dossi